    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e$4.47 a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost). The turkey breast is nearly all of it. The dumplings themselves, flour and milk and butter, cost almost nothing and turn the pot into a meal.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBuy a frozen turkey breast roast in season.\u003c/strong\u003e Around the holidays it hits its low for the year. Cook it, pull it, freeze it in bags, and dishes like this one get much cheaper for months.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eFlour, milk, butter and baking powder is the whole dumpling.\u003c/strong\u003e There is no mix to buy and no biscuit tube needed. That is the cheapest carb you can put on top of a stew.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eCarrots and celery in bags and bunches, not singles.\u003c/strong\u003e This pot goes through a lot of both, and loose produce is priced for a household of two.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eLift the lid as little as you can.\u003c/strong\u003e Every peek dumps the steam the dumplings need to cook through, and that is a free mistake to avoid."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Cook the rice separately per the package and set it aside. It goes under the stew in the containers.",
                    "Put the diced onion, sliced carrots, sliced celery and minced garlic in the slow cooker with the chicken broth, dried thyme, Italian seasoning, salt and black pepper.",
                    "Add the cooked turkey breast, put the lid on, and cook on low for 5 to 6 hours until the vegetables are tender and the broth tastes like a real stock.",
                    "Whisk together the flour, baking powder and salt, then cut in the softened butter and stir in the milk until you have a thick, sticky batter.",
                    "Turn the slow cooker to high, drop spoonfuls of the batter across the surface of the stew, and put the lid back on.",
                    "Cook 45 to 60 minutes without lifting the lid, until a dumpling comes out clean on a toothpick and the stew has thickened underneath."
                ],
